  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving, Multisectoral Emergency Assistance and Protection to Vulnerable Displaced Persons in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tigray region in Ethiopia continues to host the highest number of internally displaced persons (IDPs) primarily displaced by conflict nationwide. Many IDPs are not able to return to their area of origin, predominantly in Western Tigray. At the same time, social tensions and drought continue to displace new caseloads. The geographical focus of the response is primarily on Northwestern and Central Zones in Tigray, as well as Mekelle, which are the top three zones hosting IDPs in Tigray. Through this action, IOM is targeting newly displaced persons while ensuring minimum continuity of services in sites where the population is from Western Tigray and cannot return, prioritizing the most vulnerable cases to maximize the use of limited resources. In this action, IOM proposes is providing critical life-saving humanitarian assistance via an integrated, multisectoral response and contribute to better coordination and effectiveness of humanitarian response through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) and Shelter and Non-Food Item (SNFI), and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) Clusters.</narrative>
  </description>
